-- title:
--   Decoded executable choices reproduce the complete local schedule
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural microblock half-size $h$ and its local prime $p$. Candidates are all hash-weight tables on $512h$ binary coordinates, decoded from $p^{2(512h)}$ radix indices. The Boolean cover matrix has $p^2$ columns, one for each ordered residue pair, and records the local trimmed-cover relation. Let $I_h$ be the list of row indices selected by the prescribed number of greedy rounds, and let $w_h(i)$ decode row $i$. Then
--   $$
--   \operatorname{map}(w_h,I_h)=\operatorname{localSchedule}(h).
--   $$
--   This is equality of lists, so it preserves selection order, ties, and repeated chosen maps. It connects the machine's integer-indexed schedule to the original local-cover schedule.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightLocalCoverSchedule.lean#L77-L90

